## File 2 of 12: `frontend/app/evaluate-contract/page.tsx`

This is the upload/evaluate page. The only M2 change is a bug fix: previously `setIsLoading(false)` was in a `finally` block, which caused the form to flash back for a frame before `router.push()` completed navigation. Now loading state only resets on error.

**PR excerpt (the change):**

```typescript
// frontend/app/evaluate-contract/page.tsx:86-99
    setError(null);
    setIsLoading(true);
    try {
      const result = await evaluateContract(file, instructions, controller.signal);
      const id = crypto.randomUUID();
      setResult(id, result);
      router.push(`/contract/${id}`);
    } catch (e) {
      if (e instanceof DOMException && e.name === 'AbortError') return;
      setError('Something went wrong. Try again.');
      setIsLoading(false);
    }
```

Walk through: what was the bug, why does moving `setIsLoading(false)` from `finally` into `catch` fix it, and what happens to the loading state on the success path now? Restate in your own words.

Exactly right. On success the component unmounts via navigation — no cleanup needed.

